      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ✅ **LGTM** — All checks pass. [[trajectory](go/traj/fa060f09-849e-4972-9e9b-bbd0e4a7d172)]\n\n**Review Summary:**\n* **Functionality:** The patch accurately implements the deferral of writing to the global `fp_enc_buffer.metadata` by using stack-allocated buffers for the `nonce`, `encryption_salt`, and `tag`. The data is copied to the global state only after the key derivation and encryption process completes successfully, effectively preventing premature state mutation on intermediate failures.\n* **Security:** The security posture is robust. Generating encryption metadata into stack buffers wrapped with `CleanseWrapper` ensures these values are securely zeroed out upon exiting the scope. Additionally, the existing logic of zero-initializing `fp_enc_buffer` and cleansing it on encryption failure maintains strong defenses against memory exposure.\n* **Style:** The code follows modern C++ guidelines, correctly utilizing `std::ranges::copy` for clean and readable buffer transfers.\n* **Testing \u0026 Test Coverage:** The included Zephyr test (`test_fp_frame_v1_encrypt_template_key_derivation_failure`) thoroughly covers the failure path. By mocking `hkdf_sha256` to simulate a key derivation failure, it explicitly asserts that the `fp_enc_buffer.metadata` fields remain strictly zero-initialized.\n* **CL Size \u0026 Scope:** The CL is appropriately sized and self-contained. It focuses tightly on fixing the metadata buffer initialization without introducing unrelated refactoring.",
